    "notes": [
      "Requires xdm_android_uix_r4_media_library_consumer_workflow_overlay.zip as its direct baseline.",
      "Activity exposes Needs attention and Recent as primary views; queue decisions, queues, schedules, and recovery move into Manage activity.",
      "Settings leads with save location, smart queue, notifications, appearance, privacy/support, and About; advanced rules remain available on secondary pages.",
      "Developer options are persisted with DataStore and default to disabled. Disabling them closes the developer workspace.",
      "Runtime probes, engine matrices, Termux/aria2, media planners, dispatch/workers, privacy/cleanup, validation/release, intake/clipboard, and redacted exports are grouped behind the gate.",
      "Support reports remain available when Developer options are disabled, and all developer output retains mandatory redaction with no arbitrary shell surface.",
      "Room schema 14, versionName 0.20.0-rc08, versionCode 21, routes, engines, queue policy, schedules, recovery, external handoff, and persistence remain unchanged.",
      "UIX R6 is the next overlay and seals accessibility, responsiveness, performance, and final release validation."
    ]
